    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147-a1-a9-a10">

                <pb facs="0391" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg381"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 10 in No. 9.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Rawson to Lieutenant Low, C. S. N.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colonial Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 29, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I am directed by the governor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of your letter of yesterday’s date protesting against
                    the seizure of the Tuscaloosa, whose character you represent to be the same as
                    when, in August last, she was admitted into the port of Simon’s bay, and I am to
                    acquaint you, in reply, that a full report was submitted to her Majesty’s
                    government of all that took place on the first visit of the Tuscaloosa, and that
                    the seizure has now been made in conformity with the opinion expressed by them
                    on that report.</p>
                <p>Your protest will of course be transmitted for their consideration.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RAWSON W. RAWSON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
